{"paper": "SSC-DelhiPoliceHC-20-Oct-2022-Shift1.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 20, "tagged_count": 20, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "1434.33 cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "1435.33 cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "1437.33 cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "1436.33 cm3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "sphere-hemisphere", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "If 15 sin θ + 8 cos θ = 17, then what is the value of 15 cos θ - 8 sin θ?", "options": [{"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "0", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "Brajesh had Rs.8,600 which he invested in two parts. Simple interest received on the first part at 15% p.a. in 4 years is equal to the simple interest received on the second part at 20% p.a. in 3 years. Find the difference in the two parts.", "options": [{"text": "Rs.210", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.0", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.190", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.290", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-formula", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "Two numbers are in the ratio 2 : 3 and their LCM is 36. Find the numbers.", "options": [{"text": "12, 18", "added": false}, {"text": "12, 14", "added": false}, {"text": "10, 12", "added": false}, {"text": "14, 18", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "hcf-lcm-of-numbers", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "A retailer purchased at a rate of 11 mangoes for Rs.100 and sold at a rate of 10 mangoes for Rs.110. The percentage of profit for per mango sold is:", "options": [{"text": "21%", "added": false}, {"text": "15.5%", "added": false}, {"text": "11%", "added": false}, {"text": "22%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "articles-and-batches", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "Find the ratio between the fourth proportional of 16, 18, 8 and the mean proportional of 12, 27.", "options": [{"text": "1 : 2", "added": false}, {"text": "3 : 2", "added": false}, {"text": "2 : 5", "added": false}, {"text": "2 : 3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "proportion", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "The compound interest on Rs.15,000 at 20% per annum compounded half yearly for 1.5 year is:", "options": [{"text": "Rs.5,625", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.4,965", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.5,420", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.6,420", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Compound Interest", "sub": "compounding-frequency", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "23", "added": false}, {"text": "93", "added": false}, {"text": "35", "added": false}, {"text": "70", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "2x + 3y − 7z = 8; 3x + 2y − 8z = 7; x + y − z = 13. What is the value of x2+y2+z2?", "options": [{"text": "185", "added": false}, {"text": "205", "added": false}, {"text": "175", "added": false}, {"text": "195", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "linear-equations", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "16 days", "added": false}, {"text": "9 days", "added": false}, {"text": "12 days", "added": false}, {"text": "20 days", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": tr